{"id":46368,"date":"2026-10-05T13:32:37","date_gmt":"2026-10-05T13:32:37","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.ntop.org\/?p=46368"},"modified":"2026-10-05T21:16:39","modified_gmt":"2026-10-05T21:16:39","slug":"october-20th-join-us-for-the-ntopng-7-0-webinar","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/www.ntop.org\/october-20th-join-us-for-the-ntopng-7-0-webinar\/","title":{"rendered":"October 20th: Join us for the ntopng 7.0 Webinar"},"content":{"rendered":"<p dir=\"ltr\">Is your network monitoring keeping pace with AI, larger infrastructures, and the growing need for real observability? We&#8217;re excited to introduce <strong>ntopng 7.0<\/strong>, alongside new releases of the rest of the ntop suite.<\/p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">This is one of the biggest ntopng releases to date: a new AI-assisted analysis engine, native SIEM integration, a network-to-site hierarchy for large deployments, BGP visibility, a completely rebuilt observability\/timeseries backend on ClickHouse, and a modernized Vue.js frontend. We want to walk you through it live, with a Q&amp;A session at the end of the event.<\/p>\n<p><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/www.ntop.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/09\/Screenshot-2026-09-09-151028-1.png\" alt=\"October 20th, figure 1\" width=\"1024\" height=\"685\" \/><\/p>\n<h5 dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Here is what we will cover:<\/strong><\/h5>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li><strong>nAnalyst \u2014 AI-assisted traffic analysis.<\/strong> A brand-new chat-based assistant that lets you query live and historical flows and alerts in different languages, define AI-driven alert policies, and get AI-generated dashboards, all through an agentic loop that supports multiple LLM providers (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Qwen, and local models) plus a built-in MCP server for connecting external AI agents to ntopng.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Wazuh XDR\/SIEM integration.<\/strong> Native collection and correlation of Wazuh alerts into ClickHouse, with asset enrichment, dedicated alert pages, MITRE-mapped rules, and configurable retention, bringing SIEM-grade security visibility directly into ntopng.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Sites: hierarchy for large networks.<\/strong> A new network-to-site model designed for ISPs, MSPs, and large infrastructures, with a sites dashboard, geomap, matrix\/heatmap views, and per-site timeseries and statistics.<\/li>\n<li><strong>BGP &amp; BMP support.<\/strong> A new Looking Glass page, RPKI validation, prefix-change alerts, and full BGP context surfaced directly in live and historical flows, a big step for routing observability.<\/li>\n<li><strong>A rebuilt Observability backend.<\/strong> A new ClickHouse-based timeseries engine, including a High-Resolution counters driver, a redesigned Observability dashboard, and out-of-the-box Grafana integration.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Modern authentication &amp; a new frontend.<\/strong> SSO via OpenID Connect, Multi-Factor Authentication, Passkeys, and API key support, alongside a full migration to a Vue.js frontend with D3-based charts replacing the legacy UI.<\/li>\n<li><b>Plus<\/b>: user-defined host Tags, automatic flow deduplication, extended OT visibility (new S7comm and Profinet support), the new nEdge Lite, and a long list of performance and security hardening improvements across the board.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h5 dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Who should attend?<\/strong><\/h5>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Network engineers and SREs who want deeper, AI-assisted visibility into their infrastructure.<\/li>\n<li>Security and SOC teams looking to leverage the new Wazuh integration and AI-driven alerting.<\/li>\n<li>ISPs, service providers, and enterprises managing large, multi-site networks or their own Autonomous Systems.<\/li>\n<li>Existing ntopng users who want a guided tour of what&#8217;s new before upgrading.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h5 dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Secure your spot<\/strong><\/h5>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">The webinar is scheduled for <strong>Tuesday, October 20th, 15:00 CET \/ 9 AM EDT<\/strong>\u00a0and will be run online via Microsoft Teams. Participation is free, but space is limited: <a href=\"https:\/\/events.teams.microsoft.com\/event\/1e40da1a-beb8-411e-996f-6cc8dba4138e@03099206-608b-40d0-9032-b5cf198c536d?source=copyLinkOneEventsShareDialog\">please register at this page<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">The event will be recorded and shared with our community for those who cannot attend live.<\/p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Looking forward to seeing you there!<\/p>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Is your network monitoring keeping pace with AI, larger infrastructures, and the growing need for real observability? We&#8217;re excited to introduce ntopng 7.0, alongside new releases of the rest of the ntop\u2026<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":4,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[681,674,677,1,695,682],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-46368","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-announce","category-news","category-ntopng","category-technologies-and-trends","category-tutorials","category-webinar"],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.8 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/product\/yoast-seo-wordpress\/ -->\n<title>ntopng 7.0 Webinar on 20 October | ntop<\/title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Join the ntopng 7.0 webinar: AI, larger infrastructures and real observability, with one of the biggest ntopng releases to date.\" \/>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/www.ntop.org\/october-20th-join-us-for-the-ntopng-7-0-webinar\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"ntopng 7.0 Webinar on 20 October |